#
# READ THE LEDGER COLUMNS. `DELIVERED` is NOT a provisioning measure -- it
# increments on ANY drop while at_nest, whatever was dropped and wherever it
# came from. trailfollow's own doc carries the disproof: at gap 300 `near on`
# is 0 in all six seeds -- not one ant ever reached the food -- while `deliv
# on` reads 0, 0, 6, 4, 13, 10. A change that drives laden ants to the nest
# inflates that counter by construction, which is exactly what this one does.
#
# `ate J` is the ledger measure (ColonyBooks::diet), `came back` is the column
# 7.47's null was about, and `carry->nest` is signed cells positive homeward.

